[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Variation "Exchange Variation"]
[ECO "B13"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "bishop-trade,solid-centre"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "3.exd5"]
[Start "exchange-bd3 3...cxd5"]

4. Bd3 ( 4. Nc3 Nf6 { Develops and guards d5, which the knight on c3 attacks. } 5. Bf4 Bg4 6. f3 Bd7 ) ( 4. Nf3 { Most often reached by 2.Nf3 d5 3.exd5 cxd5 4.d4. Black answers ...Nc6, then ...e6, ...Bd6 and ...Nge7: see the 2.Nf3 line. } ) ( 4. c4 Nf6 { Develops and defends d5, and White's c4 pawn must be kept in check. } ) ( 4. Bb5+ Bd7 { Blocks with the bishop and offers a trade. Without its bishop White has nothing aiming at Black's king. } 5. Bxd7+ Nxd7 { Recaptures with a developing move. Black follows with ...e6, ...Ngf6 and ...Bd6. } ) 4... Nc6 { Develops with pressure on d4, the pawn White needs for a grip on the centre. } 5. c3 ( 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. c3 ( 6. O-O e6 ) ( 6. h3 Bxf3 { Takes the knight that guards d4. After Qxf3 nothing defends the pawn on d4: the queen has left d1 and the bishop on d3 blocks the d-file. } 7. Qxf3 Nxd4 { Wins the pawn. The knight goes back to c6 next and Black is a clean pawn up. } 8. Qf4 ( 8. Qd1 Nc6 ) 8... Nc6 ) ( 6. Be3 e6 ) 6... Qc7 7. Nbd2 Nf6 ) 5... Qc7 { Aims at the bishop on d3 and the h2 pawn, and stops Bf4: White's bishop would hang to the queen. } 6. Ne2 Bg4 { Gets the bishop out before ...e6 shuts it in, and it eyes the knight on e2, which guards the d4 pawn. } 7. O-O e6 { Supports d5 and opens a path for the f8 bishop. } 8. f3 Bh5 { Keeps the bishop alive: from h5 it can swing to g6 and trade White's good bishop. } 9. Nd2 Nf6 { Brings the last knight out, so Black is fully developed. } 10. Nb3 Bd6 { Eyes the kingside. Black's plan: trade the light bishops with ...Bg6, castle, and play for a safe, equal position. If White leaves the book, castle and aim at d4 with the pieces. } *
